# InventorySystem Module — Project Memory

Self-contained inventory + equipment + drag/drop package for **Unity 6000.4.9f1**, **UI Toolkit only** (no uGUI).
Designed like an Asset Store package: `Assets/InventorySystem/` can be copied into any project; `Demo/` and `Scripts/Extras/` are deletable.
Last relevant commits: `530ceeb partial InventorySystem refactor`, `725d330 added DemoMat`. Refactor is described as *partial* — expect leftovers (see "Known quirks").

## Assemblies (compiler-enforced boundaries)

| asmdef | Namespace | References | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `Scripts/InventorySystem.asmdef` | `InventorySystem` | none (engine only) | `autoReferenced: true`. Must NEVER reference game code (`Assembly-CSharp`). |
| `Demo/InventorySystem.Demos.asmdef` | `InventorySystem.Demos` | `InventorySystem`, `Unity.InputSystem` | Demo only. Core must not depend on Input System. |
| `Editor/InventorySystem.Editor.asmdef` | `InventorySystem.Editor` | `InventorySystem` | Editor only. `InventorySystemMenu`: *GameObject > Inventory System > Inventory UI* instantiates the `InventoryUI` prefab (found by name + `InventoryUIController`, prefers `/Starter/`), scoped to the target scene: asks if that scene already has an `InventoryUIController`, removes the instance's `InventoryModel`/`EquipmentController` if that scene already has one. |

Game code (`Assembly-CSharp`) consumes the module with `using InventorySystem;`. Dependency direction is one-way: game → module.

